This is a Linux dev branch.
The heresy has been purged. There is no windows support for this version.


**Status: Not ready for use.**

This repository is a work-in-progress port/migration of gVRMod from OpenVR to native OpenXR.

### Current State
- **Only Linux is supported.**
- **Not ready for use **

### What works
- Submitting stolen texture from OpenGL to OpenXR VR compositor
- Head tracking
- Per-eye render targets (separate left/right RTs)
- OpenXR interaction profile bindings (Oculus Touch / Index / KHR simple)
- Analog→boolean threshold for triggers/grips (Quest has no trigger/click)
- **In-game controller binding UI** (`vrmod_bindingeditor`) — SteamVR binding UI replacement
  - Physical sources → logical actions, including **chords** (AND of multiple buttons)
  - Saved to `garrysmod/data/vrmod/vrmod_openxr_bindings.json`

### What doesn't / WIP
- Rendering still imperfect (stereo crop / orientation tuning ongoing)
- Stick/vector rebinding not in the UI yet (walk/turn stay on OpenXR defaults)
- Full body tracker poses untested
- Driving action set shares short names with main (first-match binding)

### Challenges

- OpenXR has no SteamVR-style binding UI or chord API; rebinding is a Lua layer over fixed hardware sources.
- SteamVR binding JSON is not consumed by OpenXR.

### What this repo contains
- Native module source (C++) targeting OpenXR + Linux (GLX + togl)
- Client-side addon under `addon/gvrmod/`
- Build and install scripts

### Installation
See `./install.sh`. It will:
- Build the native module
- Install the module + OpenXR loader bundle
- Delete any existing `gvrmod` folder under `garrysmod/addons/`
- Install a fresh copy of the addon from `addon/gvrmod/`

Run `./install.sh --help` for options.

### Uninstall
```bash
./install.sh --uninstall
```

### Important Notes
- You need a working OpenXR runtime (e.g. Monado + WiVRn).
- The install script will attempt to bundle the OpenXR loader and its dependencies.
- This is an experimental development branch.

